{
  "id": 172,
  "Specification": "A specification of the single-lane bridge concurrency problem. A bridge supports only one direction of traffic at a time; cars from the same direction may share the bridge, but two cars from opposite directions on the bridge constitute a safety violation. Models car movement, queueing before the bridge, and uses weak fairness to verify safety invariants and liveness properties (cars eventually enter and exit the bridge).",
